        "canonical_content_text": "- Payrolls: **+165K** (total nonfarm 159,293K vs 159,128K for September as now published). - Unemployment rate: **4.1%** (September 4.2%). The frozen Strong branch needed payrolls about +154K or more and unemployment 4.2% or lower. Both held (+165K, 4.1%). The Weak branch failed.\n\na hawkish labour surprise raises the expected Fed path, the USD and real yields; a second weak print after September's +29K lowers the expected hike path and weakens the USD; Whipsaw after the release and the weekend gap no separate rates read was taken in this run. No market-context.json was gathered.",
